WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.380
The neural crest supplies nerve cells outside the brain and spinal cord, the glia

2
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.380
that wrap nerves, pigment cells, and bone and cartilage of the face.

3
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.380
These tissues share an embryonic ancestor.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.620
Crest cells form at the edge of the neural plate, then leave and migrate through the

5
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:26.300
embryo. That shared origin explains why gut neurons, hair pigment and hearing can

6
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.220
fail together. Where along the body they start helps determine what they eventually

7
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.220
become.

8
00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:35.583
In the head, crest makes facial bone and cartilage.

9
00:00:36.643 --> 00:00:40.263
Vagal and sacral crest supplies neurons and glia of the gut wall.

10
00:00:41.243 --> 00:00:45.583
Trunk crest gives sensory and sympathetic neurons, Schwann cells and melanocytes.

11
00:00:46.563 --> 00:00:50.023
In birds and mammals, trunk crest does not normally make skeleton.

12
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.337
First, cells need a crest identity.

13
00:00:54.257 --> 00:01:00.937
In one proposed network, BMP, Wnt and FGF signals turn on border genes, then crest

14
00:01:00.937 --> 00:01:05.037
genes. These control adhesion, movement and later fate.

15
00:01:06.077 --> 00:01:09.977
Crest cells loosen their grip on neighbours, lose their top-to-bottom polarity,

16
00:01:10.497 --> 00:01:12.777
break through the basement membrane and crawl away.

17
00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:18.097
That change, from a cell in a sheet to a free mesenchymal cell, is an

18
00:01:18.097 --> 00:01:20.217
epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition.

19
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:22.217
EMT.

20
00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:26.027
Migration depends on the surroundings and on other cells.

21
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:31.427
In the chick trunk, one route runs through the somites, the tissue blocks beside the

22
00:01:31.427 --> 00:01:36.347
neural tube. It gives sensory and sympathetic ganglia and adrenal medulla.

23
00:01:37.207 --> 00:01:40.167
A later route under the skin gives mostly melanocytes.

24
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.250
Crest cells also steer each other.

25
00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:48.810
In frog and zebrafish, cells that touch stop moving towards each other and head off

26
00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:49.810
in new directions.

27
00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.310
In frog cranial crest, mutual attraction keeps the group together, while a chemical

28
00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:56.450
cue helps guide it.

29
00:01:57.190 --> 00:02:00.970
How far this applies to trunk crest in birds and mammals is less clear.

30
00:02:01.933 --> 00:02:05.353
When crest development fails, several tissues can be affected.

31
00:02:06.293 --> 00:02:09.733
In Hirschsprung disease, crest fails to colonise the distal gut.

32
00:02:10.653 --> 00:02:14.793
In Waardenburg syndrome, pigment changes and hearing loss can occur together.

33
00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:19.513
Some patients have both conditions from a mutation in a single gene.

34
00:02:20.393 --> 00:02:24.053
Their different symptoms point back to a shared developmental ancestry.
